00:04:28.900 --> 00:04:30.354
Part three: grammar.

74
00:04:31.217 --> 00:04:35.515
Grammar focus: Future perfect for long-term predictions.

75
00:04:35.815 --> 00:04:36.979
Look at the pattern.

76
00:04:37.683 --> 00:04:42.191
By 2035, technology will have transformed many careers.

77
00:04:43.083 --> 00:04:45.489
By then, I will have learned coding.

78
00:04:46.383 --> 00:04:50.473
By 2040, robots will have replaced many factory jobs.

79
00:04:51.433 --> 00:04:56.219
Use the future perfect for an action that will be complete before a time in the future.

80
00:04:56.983 --> 00:05:02.782
Be careful! Don't say: By 2035, technology will transformed many careers.

81
00:05:04.733 --> 00:05:10.053
Say: By 2035, technology will have transformed many careers.

82
00:05:10.353 --> 00:05:13.584
The future perfect is 'will have' + past participle.

